        "title": "On Masters Saturday, we’ll stay indoors and tour the Champions locker room. Former Masters winners have their own Champions Locker room, located on the second floor of the original Manor House, near the stairs from the Crow’s Nest. The Champions’ Locker Room is not as spacious as you might imagine: Masters winners share its 28 oak lockers, as allocated by the club. On arriving at Augusta, past champs find their green jackets hanging up, ready and waiting (one of Augusta’s rules is that green jackets may only be worn at Augusta National, apart from by the reigning champion, who is entitled to wear the jacket away from the club until the following year’s Masters). Tiger Woods shares a locker with the late Jackie Burke Jr., Spieth with the late Arnold Palmer, Sergio with Olazabal. Three card tables with comfortable club chairs fill the room, but the view off the adjoining veranda can’t be beat: it looks out onto Magnolia Lane and the Founders Circle. =========================== #golfclubhouses #whyilovethisgame #clubhouse #beautifulgolfcourses #countryclub #golfgeorgia #georgiagolf #masters #themasters #masterstournament #masters2023 #masters2022 #augustanational #agnc @",
